{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Forty years old.</b> Esav is compared to a pig, as it says ״יְכַרְסְמֶנָּה חֲזִיר מִיָּעַר״ (Psalms 80). This pig, when it lies down, stretches out its hooves, as if to say: See, I am clean. So too these rob and extort and present themselves as fit. For all forty years Esav would seize women from under their husbands and ravish them. When he was forty he said: My father married a wife at forty years old — I too will do likewise."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:42.223770877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}